<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PermissionSet xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        PermissionSet.Description is capped at 255 characters. The full rationale below is
        security-relevant and was moved here rather than deleted; a comment is repo-only and
        is never sent to the Metadata API, so it can be as long as it needs to be. Do not
        paste this back into <description> verbatim - trim it if it needs to change there.

        Read-only access to the IR-record-type Lead/Contact/Account population only, full FLS
        on the standard fields IR needs. For the Principal, who sees IR records through the
        role hierarchy but needs the matching object permission to use it. Deliberately NO
        viewAllRecords - visibility comes from the role hierarchy above
        Investor_Relations_Manager, not from this permission set. Carries no broker field and
        no acquisitions Lead deal-screening field.

        =====================================================================
        ADDED 2026-08-16 - Offering__c, read-only counterpart to DPEG_IR_Edit's grant.
        =====================================================================
        See DPEG_IR_Edit's comment for the full rationale (FSD Gap Tranche 1, Q1.2 follow-up,
        user directive: "give them read/write permission"). This set is the READ-ONLY layer-3
        twin - allowRead=true only on Offering__c, readable-only FLS on its three fields. No
        viewAllRecords, matching every other grant on this set; record access for a row this
        persona does not own comes from the Offering_IR_Visibility owner-based sharing rule
        (Offering__c.sharingRules-meta.xml), not from this permission set.

        Reconciled against usman-dpeg via sf project retrieve (2026-08-16) before this edit:
        the live set carried NO Offering__c objectPermissions or fieldPermissions entries at
        all, matching the repo file, so this is a pure addition with nothing org-side at risk
        of being replaced.
    -->
